{"id":"2026-11-22-CDW","date":"2026-11-22","ticker":"CDW","name":"CDW","sector":"Information Technology","industry":"Information Technology Services","price":161.78,"price_date":"2026-11-20","timeframe_days":182,"headline":"CDW's sales growth sped up to 18% on AI server and storage demand, and management raised its yearly earnings growth target twice in two quarters","side":"long","timeframe":"About 6 months, through the next two quarterly reports","thesis":"CDW's sales grew 18% from a year ago in the September quarter to $6.8B, up from 10% in June, as businesses spent on servers and storage to run AI. Storage and servers more than doubled, and laptop and desktop sales rose 19% as companies replaced old machines. Management raised its full-year earnings per share growth target for the second quarter in a row, from 4% to 6% at the start of the year to 7% to 9% in August and now 10% to 13%. Adjusted earnings per share rose 20% to $3.26, well above the high single digits management had expected. The stock trades at 14.7 times earnings, below its median of 17.9, so the market is treating this as a short burst. If the upgrade cycle lasts into 2027, the multiple has room to recover.","wrong_if":"A close under 144 would break below the late October gap and the 50-day average, and the idea would be over. It is also wrong if CDW guides 2027 sales growth back to low single digits or if gross margin keeps falling, which would mean the extra sales are coming from low-profit hardware only.","business":"CDW is a reseller of technology to businesses, governments, schools and hospitals in the US, the UK and Canada. It buys laptops, servers, storage, networking gear and software licenses from makers like Dell, HP, Cisco and Microsoft, and sells and installs them for customers that lack big IT teams. It earns a markup on each sale plus fees for setup and support services. Its customers range from small firms to large companies and public agencies.","segments_note":"Business customers, the largest group at $4.0B, grew 21% in the September quarter, up from 9% in June. UK and Canada grew 26%, the fastest group, and government grew 10%. Education was the slowest at 8% but improved from 1% in June. Every customer group sped up or held steady, so the gain is broad. By product, hardware grew 21% and software 14%, while services grew only 2%.","growth_note":"Sales were $6.8B, up 18% against 10% in June. Gross margin was 20.5%, 1.4 points lower than a year ago because more of the sales were low-margin hardware, though it rose 0.4 points from June. Operating margin was 7.2% and operating income rose 17% to $620M. Gross profit grew about 10%, slower than sales, so the profit gain is real but smaller than the sales headline. Free cash flow was more than $500M in the quarter.","commentary":[{"point":"Sales grew 18% to $6.8B with record hardware and software sales. Hardware grew 21%, storage and servers more than doubled, laptops and desktops rose 19% and software rose 14%.","speaker":"Chris Leahy, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Raised the full-year earnings per share growth target to 10% to 13%, from 7% to 9% in August and 4% to 6% at the start of the year, and raised gross profit growth to mid-to-high single digits.","speaker":"Al Miralles, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Adjusted earnings per share were $3.26, up 20%, well above their plan of high single-digit growth. Operating income rose 17% to $620M.","speaker":"Al Miralles, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Higher-value products such as servers and storage were a record 38.2% of gross profit, up 2.2 points from a year ago.","speaker":"Al Miralles, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"number"},{"point":"Said AI adoption by businesses is pushing strong spending on infrastructure, and that the team executed with precision to deliver record results.","speaker":"Chris Leahy, CEO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"},{"point":"Said the lower gross margin came from selling more of certain products, not from cutting prices on the same products. Sounded excited about the Lovelytics data consulting purchase.","speaker":"Al Miralles, CFO","call":"Q3 2026","kind":"tone"}],"tone_note":"Tone jumped over the last three calls, with net tone going from 56 to 97 to 107. The answers to analysts were 42 points more upbeat than on the call before, and management dodged no questions. That fits a company raising its targets with the numbers already in hand.","technical_note":"The stock closed at 161.78, above its 50-day average (152.55) and well above its 200-day average (135.79). It ran to a 52-week high of 175.19 after the report and has pulled back to the middle of its 20-day range of about 150 to 173, which brought RSI down to 51 from overheated levels. Over six months it beat the S&P 500 by 58 points and tech stocks by 77. Volume is normal.","valuation_note":"At 14.7 times trailing earnings, CDW is below its median of 17.9. A return to the median on another year of 10% earnings growth would put the stock well above the target. The discount reflects worry that the AI hardware wave will end, so this idea needs 2027 guidance to show growth holding.","levels":{"entry_lo":154,"entry_hi":165,"stop":144,"target":192,"note":"Buy between 154 and 165, around the 50-day average and the middle of the post-earnings range. The stop at 144 is under the 20-day low of about 150 and about two daily ranges below the 50-day average. The target of 192 is about 10% above the 52-week high and assumes the multiple moves part of the way back toward its median. From the posted price that is about $30 of upside for $18 of risk, or 1.7 to 1."},"risks":["The AI hardware surge may pull purchases forward, leaving a gap in 2027.","Gross margin is lower for the year because hardware is a bigger share of sales; more of that would cap profit growth.","Net debt is about 2.5 times yearly operating profit, which limits how much it can buy back.","Memory and chip shortages could raise costs or delay shipments of servers and laptops.","Not known from the brief: 2027 guidance, the date of the next report, and how much of the growth is a one-time Windows upgrade cycle."],"catalysts":["The December quarter report, likely early February 2027, with the first 2027 outlook.","Dell, HP and Cisco earnings, which show whether server, storage and PC demand is holding.","Federal and state budget timing, since government is about 14% of sales."],"facts":{"financials":{"updated":"2026-11-18","adj_eps_name":"Non-GAAP EPS","quarters":[{"q":"Dec '23","id":"FY2023Q4","end":"2023-12-31","rev":5018.5,"gm":23.0,"om":8.7,"nm":5.9,"eps":2.18,"adj_eps":2.57,"rev_yoy":-7.7,"eps_yoy":2.8},{"q":"Mar '24","id":"FY2024Q1","end":"2024-03-31","rev":4872.7,"gm":21.8,"om":6.7,"nm":4.4,"eps":1.59,"adj_eps":1.92,"rev_yoy":-4.5,"eps_yoy":-5.4},{"q":"Jun '24","id":"FY2024Q2","end":"2024-06-30","rev":5423.4,"gm":21.8,"om":8.0,"nm":5.2,"eps":2.07,"adj_eps":2.5,"rev_yoy":-3.6,"eps_yoy":-2.3},{"q":"Sep '24","id":"FY2024Q3","end":"2024-09-30","rev":5516.6,"gm":21.8,"om":8.7,"nm":5.7,"eps":2.34,"adj_eps":2.63,"rev_yoy":-2.0,"eps_yoy":-3.3},{"q":"Dec '24","id":"FY2024Q4","end":"2024-12-31","rev":5186,"gm":22.3,"om":7.9,"nm":5.1,"eps":1.97,"adj_eps":2.48,"rev_yoy":3.3,"eps_yoy":-3.5},{"q":"Mar '25","id":"FY2025Q1","end":"2025-03-31","rev":5199.1,"gm":21.6,"om":7.0,"nm":4.3,"eps":1.69,"adj_eps":2.15,"rev_yoy":6.7,"eps_yoy":12.0},{"q":"Jun '25","id":"FY2025Q2","end":"2025-06-30","rev":5976.6,"gm":20.8,"om":7.0,"nm":4.5,"eps":2.05,"adj_eps":2.6,"rev_yoy":10.2,"eps_yoy":4.0},{"q":"Sep '25","id":"FY2025Q3","end":"2025-09-30","rev":5737.4,"gm":21.9,"om":7.7,"nm":5.1,"eps":2.21,"adj_eps":2.71,"rev_yoy":4.0,"eps_yoy":3.0},{"q":"Dec '25","id":"FY2025Q4","end":"2025-12-31","rev":5511,"gm":22.8,"om":7.8,"nm":5.1,"eps":2.14,"adj_eps":2.57,"rev_yoy":6.3,"eps_yoy":3.6},{"q":"Mar '26","id":"FY2026Q1","end":"2026-03-31","rev":5679.8,"gm":21.0,"om":6.6,"nm":4.1,"eps":1.82,"adj_eps":2.28,"rev_yoy":9.2,"e